core_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.5039505860561426,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.00986480681616328,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":22.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.04098372362050662,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":31.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.05053,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":33.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Intuitive Machines, Inc. operates as a space infrastructure and services company in the United States. The company provides delivery services for the transportation and delivery of payloads, such as satellites, scientific instruments, and cargo to various destinations in space, rideshare delivery, and lunar surface access; data transmission services, which include the collection, processing, and interpretation of space-based data, as well as utilizing AI applications, such as command, control, communications, reconnaissance and prospecting; and infrastructure as a service solutions for navigation, maintenance, scientific data collection, and system health monitoring. It also offers Nova-C lunar lander that combines flight-proven with a scalable design to meet the demands of the emerging lunar economy; Micro Nova Hopper develops propulsive drone that is designed to land, deploy, and hop on the company's IM-2 mission; and Nova-D developed to transport critical payloads, including infrastructure services, such as fission surface power systems, lunar terrain vehicles, and rovers enabling sustainable lunar exploration and development. In addition, the company provides lunar data network. It serves its products to the U.S. government, which include NASA, national security space, U.S. department of Defense, and state governments; commercial; and international customers. The company was founded in 2013 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Stephen J. Altemus | Co-Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 525 people. Revenue per employee of $400K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 63%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $16K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Intuitive Machines, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $2.1B market cap on $210M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +63% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -63% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $56M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -20.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (27.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 50% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $170.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 310% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Is Intuitive Machines (NASDAQ:LUNR) Gaining Space Market Attention?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/industrial/why-is-intuitive-machines-nasdaqlunr-gaining-space-market-attention","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794588180.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title